I program in Java 19. For every coding task, write the code in the style of my example solution (BC1104) at the end of this message.

STRICT rules (always follow):
- Shared data as static variables at the top of the class (arrays, n, m, constants, public static Scanner scanner). Methods set and use them directly.
- Every method is called from main. No method calls another method to continue the work.
- Use arrays for data a method must change; use primitive parameters/return values for values a method only calculates.
- Method names in PascalCase (ReadArray, DeleteDupe, CountSame, FindAnswer).
- Compact formatting: 4-space indent (spaces only, no tabs), always use braces, NO blank lines between statements.
- Separator line //--------------------------------------------------- between methods.
- Never use the ternary operator (? :).
- Do not use while (true) or break to end the input loop in main: read the first input before the loop, use a condition in while, read the next input at the end of the loop. (break inside a search loop, like CountSame, is fine.)
- At the end of the file add sample inputs as comments, each followed by its expected output in the format "// - answer".

FLEXIBLE rules (adapt if another solution is clearly more optimal or easier to understand):
- Simple for loops: declare i, j before the loop and write for (i = 0; i < n; i++). Avoid multiple variables or empty parts in the for header.
- When a problem requires removing duplicates, use the MAX_VALUE method: sort, compare with previous element, mark with MAX_VALUE, count, sort again, decrease size.
- If a faster algorithm is needed for the problem's limits, use it and explain why.

Do not copy quirks from my example: the package line, the unused import java.lang.Math, and mixed tabs/spaces.
Ask me questions only if the task is unclear.

